Deadline and readiness interpretation
The scripted successful completion again occurs immediately; Foundation completion/invalidation is delayed until about 4.347s, and the final deadline check rejects the already-expired operation. The response callbacks in shared success/deinit occur after their watchdogs fired and correctly reject cancelled work. Active-trickle task dispatch takes about 1.795545s; readiness expires at 2.137235s from task creation, before any admitted body, so its 120ms active watchdog is never armed.
The silent120ms watchdog fires at 0.126167s, but task completion arrives at 4.369519s, followed promptly by invalidation/tail/caller wake. Unlike diagnostic11, the major silent-request gap here is before completion delivery, and its original under-two-second assertion fails. Prompt cancellation signalling alone is not proof of timely joined completion. This run cannot support a claim that the HTTPS cancellation deadline is fully qualified under this instrumented load.

